BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-nodes-rfp-local-compute@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute AI Nodes RFP\, Track I: Local Compute
DESCRIPTION:Track I of Foresight Institute's AI for Science & Safety Nodes 
 RFP funds building and scaling local compute setups that individuals or co
 mmunities physically own and control. With five companies holding 71 perce
 nt of the world's AI compute\, researchers relying on APIs and rented comp
 ute face data exposure\, steep price increases and the risk of losing acce
 ss altogether\; open models are ready for serious science and safety work\
 , but the ecosystem lacks sovereign and secure compute infrastructure. LOO
 KING FOR: local compute clusters in different sizes and configurations tha
 t are easy to set up and run across varied connectivity and electricity en
 vironments\; blueprints for easy yet secure cluster management\; models fo
 r bringing down cost\, like selling idle compute or connecting to communit
 y clusters\; ideally a business case for building\, selling and distributi
 ng such clusters at scale. EXAMPLE DELIVERABLES: a prototype AI cluster an
  average person can deploy at home\, software that runs a node without exp
 ert knowledge\, economic models showing how the hardware pays for itself\,
  a pilot deployment for individuals or communities. Selected projects rece
 ive grant funding\, private local compute\, workspace at the San Francisco
  or Berlin AI Nodes\, travel-paid field-building events and access to Fore
 sight's advisors and network\; in-person contributors at the Nodes are str
 ongly prioritised. Individuals\, teams\, and nonprofit or for-profit organ
 isations worldwide may apply (for-profits must justify their need for gran
 t funding). Deadline 31 October 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisation: Foresig
 ht Institute\nLocation: Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
 \nAward: Typically $30\,000 to $100\,000 per grant (larger possible for th
 e right project)\, plus private local compute and workspace at the San Fra
 ncisco or Berlin AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\n\
 nMore: https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-local-comp
 ute/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-local-compute/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-nodes-rfp-coordination-accountability@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute AI Nodes RFP\, Track II: Coordination
  and Accountability
DESCRIPTION:Track II of Foresight Institute's AI for Science & Safety Nodes
  RFP funds ways for increasingly capable AI systems to coordinate with eac
 h other\, the people using them\, and the wider world\, without handing po
 wer to a single model\, lab or government. THREE FOCUS AREAS: (1) Supercol
 laboration and decentralized alignment: coordination and credit-assignment
  protocols\, tooling for massive human-AI collectives\, incentive designs 
 robust to gaming\, mutual monitoring and cross-checking among agents\, sca
 lable verification\, and open coordination protocols built on boundaries a
 s Schelling points for multi-agent coordination. (2) Human Empowerment: ev
 idence\, decision rules and working tools for when human control genuinely
  empowers people versus when AI delegation is preferable\, including a 'wh
 en to defer control' framework and mechanisms to detect and fix hollow ove
 rsight. (3) AI Insurance and Open Governance: building a middle layer betw
 een lab self-governance and government regulation\, such as ways for insur
 ers to judge and price frontier-lab risk\, independent incident reporting 
 and assessment that does not leak lab secrets\, and mechanisms like develo
 per mutuals\, catastrophe bonds or liability for near-misses. Selected pro
 jects receive grant funding\, private local compute\, workspace at the San
  Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes\, travel-paid field-building events and acce
 ss to Foresight's advisors and network\; in-person contributors at the Nod
 es are strongly prioritised. Individuals\, teams\, and nonprofit or for-pr
 ofit organisations worldwide may apply (for-profits must justify their nee
 d for grant funding). Deadline 31 October 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco a
 nd Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,000 to $100\,000 per grant\, with smalle
 r amounts for the Human Empowerment and AI Insurance & Open Governance foc
 us areas\; plus private local compute and workspace at the San Francisco o
 r Berlin AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: h
 ttps://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-coordination-and-a
 ccountability/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-coordination-a
 nd-accountability/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-nodes-rfp-ai-first-science@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute AI Nodes RFP\, Track III: AI-First Sc
 ience (Bio\, Neuro\, Nano)
DESCRIPTION:Track III of Foresight Institute's AI for Science & Safety Node
 s RFP funds AI-first science in bio\, neuro and nano: work that asks what 
 important science is stuck\, what it is actually stuck on\, and whether we
  can build the thing that removes that constraint. THREE FOCUS AREAS: (1) 
 Automated nanotechnology: AI methods for nanoscale design\, simulation and
  assembly\, closed-loop fabrication and characterization tools\, credible 
 application pathways from toy problems to medicine\, environment and botto
 m-up production\, and defensive applications and safety frameworks. (2) Wh
 ole-brain emulation: cheaper and faster brain mapping and preservation\, b
 ringing down the cost of connectomics through better imaging or cheaper pr
 oofreading\, lo-fi emulation pathways that predict organism behavior from 
 behavioral and neural data\, and shorter experimental feedback loops in ne
 urobiology. (3) Replacement\, Enhancement\, Biostasis: longevity work incl
 uding tissue engineering\, organ synthesis\, 3D bioprinting and progressiv
 e replacement strategies\; reversible biostasis for organs and full humans
  with improved preservation and revival protocols and organ banking\; and 
 datasets for independently testing genetic predictors\, gene editing and b
 etter measures of aging. Selected projects receive grant funding\, private
  local compute\, workspace at the San Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes\, trave
 l-paid field-building events and access to Foresight's advisors and networ
 k\; in-person contributors at the Nodes are strongly prioritised. Individu
 als\, teams\, and nonprofit or for-profit organisations worldwide may appl
 y (for-profits must justify their need for grant funding). Deadline 31 Oct
 ober 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisation: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Rem
 ote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,000
  to $100\,000 per grant\, with higher amounts for this track than the Huma
 n Empowerment and AI Insurance areas (larger possible for the right projec
 t)\; plus private local compute and workspace at the San Francisco or Berl
 in AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: https:/
 /foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-ai-first-science/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-ai-first-scien
 ce/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
