DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Research
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Research scheme contributes to the costs 
 of a research project or artist-in-residency that feeds the development of
  new work and benefits The Hague's art climate. WHO CAN APPLY: The Hague a
 rtists registered in the Stroom database with an updated profile (Mijn Str
 oom)\, and also curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and others pro
 fessionally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from outside
  The Hague submit a CV for consideration. APPLICATION: via the Stroom port
 al using Stroom's budget model\, with amounts excluding VAT. NOT ELIGIBLE:
  applicants enrolled in (art) educational programmes (Bachelor\, Master\, 
 postdoc\, PhD) or art academy students\, and post-academic work periods su
 ch as the Rijksakademie\, De Ateliers\, the Jan van Eyck Academie and the 
 EKWC fall outside the funding scheme system. DEADLINE: the last 2026 round
  closes 25 October 2026 (rounds recur roughly every six weeks). The grant 
 is valid for up to two years after the decision\, with 80 percent paid upf
 ront.\n\nOrganisation: Stroom Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands.
  Open to Hague artists registered with Stroom and to curators\, mediators\
 , critics\, publicists and others professionally active in the contemporar
 y art world\; applicants from outside The Hague apply with a CV.\nAward: M
 aximum EUR 5\,000 per research project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant p
 er calendar year. Amounts exclude VAT and grants are only awarded on demon
 strable financial need. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the
  grant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with
  80 percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https
 ://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-research?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-resea
 rch?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to Hague artists registered with Str
 oom and to curators\, mediators\, critics\, publicists and others professi
 onally active in the contemporary art world\; applicants from outside The 
 Hague apply with a CV.
END:VEVENT
