UID:onx-seeds-soft-circuits-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: Onassis ONX: ONX Seeds 2026\, Soft Circuits for Hard Time
 s (Athens\, hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:ONX Seeds 2026 is a four-month incubation and seed funding prog
 ram run by Onassis ONX\, the Onassis Foundation's platform for art and adv
 anced technologies\, hosted in Athens in a hybrid format under the theme S
 oft Circuits for Hard Times. It invites emerging artists\, creative techno
 logists\, designers\, game makers\, performers\, sound and visual artists 
 and makers (individuals\, groups and collectives\, Greek and international
 ) to develop early-stage prototypes that make the digital tangible: intera
 ctive objects\, wearable or embedded systems\, screen-based worlds\, parti
 cipatory environments\, games\, rituals\, sonic works\, moving images and 
 hybrid analogue-digital forms. Proposals should be realistic in scope and 
 result in an exhibitable prototype. SUPPORT: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed fun
 ding per project\, weekly technical mentoring plus curatorial and business
  mentoring and online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams (remote participation for everyone else)\,
  presentation at ONX Exhibition Athens (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\,
  accommodation and artwork transport covered for non-Athens participants\,
  and connections to the ONX network in Athens\, New York and beyond. HOW T
 O APPLY: via the Onassis open calls portal\, with project summary\, concep
 t\, visitor experience\, technical requirements\, production plan and bio\
 , plus a mood board or project deck\, portfolio and development budget as 
 single PDFs\; technical documentation and links to demos or repositories o
 ptional. DEADLINE: 26 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Onassis ONX (Onassis 
 Foundation)\nLocation: Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators f
 rom Greece and internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams
 .\nAward: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000 seed funding per project\, set by scope\; u
 p to four projects selected. Plus weekly technical\, curatorial and busine
 ss mentoring\, online masterclasses\, studio and equipment access at Onass
 is Ready for Athens-based teams\, and presentation at ONX Exhibition Athen
 s (17 to 21 March 2027) with travel\, accommodation and artwork transport 
 covered for non-Athens participants. No application fee.\nDuration: Four-m
 onth incubation\, culminating in ONX Exhibition Athens\, 17 to 21 March 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-har
 d-times-2?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://opencalls.onassis.org/onx-seeds-soft-circuits-for-hard-times-2?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Athens\, Greece\, hybrid format. Open to creators from Greece and 
 internationally\; remote participation for non-Athens teams.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:make-a-thek-mobility-knowledge-exchange-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: make-a-thek: Mobility Scheme & Knowledge Exchange Program
 me (Europe + pilot countries)
DESCRIPTION:make-a-thek\, a Horizon Europe project (grant No. 101177660) co
 ordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, connects creative spaces\, public
  libraries and makers across Europe and beyond to share skills in circular
  fashion\, traditional crafts and technology. Its open call runs two track
 s. MOBILITY SCHEME (Track A): experienced practitioners (make-a-thek Exper
 ts) travel to an EU pilot location (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapes
 t\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv or Zaporizhzhia) t
 o deliver a workshop\, talk or hands-on training\, with a EUR 1\,000 stipe
 nd to support expenses. KNOWLEDGE EXCHANGE PROGRAMME (Track B): learners\,
  practitioners\, makers\, craftspeople and librarians travel to a 2-day in
 -person group meet-up (Cohort 1 in Barcelona between end of November and s
 tart of December 2026\; Cohort 2 in Berlin in May 2027)\, then organise a 
 local knowledge-sharing activity\, with a EUR 850 stipend. Up to 12 partic
 ipants per track annually. ELIGIBILITY: legal residents of EU member state
 s\, Horizon Europe associated countries\, or the international pilot count
 ries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, the Philippines and Chile\; propos
 als must align with at least one focus area: Circular Fashion\, Digitising
  Traditional Crafts\, or Open Technologies. HOW TO APPLY: via the Typeform
  linked from the open call page. The early-bird round closed 15 September 
 2026\; late applications are accepted until 1 December 2026\, and the next
  call runs 1 February to 31 March 2027. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026.\n\nOrga
 nisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, funded b
 y Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barc
 elona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\,
  Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) an
 d Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon
  Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Afric
 a\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: EUR 1\,000
  flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange Programme:
  EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, workshops or 2-
 day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start of Decembe
 r 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Buda
 pest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)
 \; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). 
 Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon Europe associated co
 untries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, Phili
 ppines and Chile.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:visual-imaginaries-gender-uva-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Visual Imaginaries of Gender: Paid Student Research Assis
 tantships in Art and Generative AI (Amsterdam)
DESCRIPTION:NOTE: this is a paid student research assistantship (a 0.2 FTE 
 appointment) rather than a grant\, and only currently enrolled students ar
 e eligible. Four student research assistants with a background in art\, de
 sign or related fields are sought for a three-month research project on ge
 nder representation in text-to-image generative AI systems. The project tr
 eats artistic production as a research method: generative AI models increa
 singly shape contemporary visual culture\, and these systems reflect\, rep
 roduce\, and sometimes challenge cultural assumptions about identity\, gen
 der\, and social roles. ROLE: each assistant develops an individual artist
 ic exploration of gender representation in generative AI\, with considerab
 le creative freedom in approach\, themes\, prompts\, and modes of experime
 ntation\; documents their creative and research process\; participates in 
 periodic group discussions and research meetings\; and contributes to coll
 ective reflection on the project's findings. OUTCOMES: the four art projec
 ts will be presented in a collective exhibition on the theme 'Visual Imagi
 naries of Gender in Generative AI'\, and the students' documented experien
 ces and reflections will feed into an academic publication taking an auto-
 ethnographic perspective on artistic engagement with generative AI. Applic
 ations are particularly encouraged from students interested in the interse
 ction of art\, technology\, critical inquiry\, and questions of gender and
  representation. APPLICATION: send a motivation letter and art portfolio t
 o Piera Riccio (p.riccio@uva.nl). DEADLINE: 25 September 2026.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: University of Amsterdam (Visual Imaginaries of Gender project\, Pier
 a Riccio)\nLocation: Amsterdam\, Netherlands. Applicants must be enrolled 
 as a student to be eligible.\nAward: Approximately EUR 600 per month\, app
 roximately EUR 1\,800 over the full three-month project\, for a 0.2 FTE ap
 pointment (about 8 hours per week). Four positions. No application fee.\nD
 uration: 3 months\, October to December 2026\, at 0.2 FTE (approximately 8
  hours per week).\n\nMore: https://multix.io/visual-imaginaries-vacancy.ht
 ml?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://multix.io/visual-imaginaries-vacancy.html?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands. Applicants must be enrolled as a student 
 to be eligible.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cité internationale des arts Residency\, 7
 th Call (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The 7th call of the Art Explora residency programme at the Cit
 é internationale des arts opened 21 September 2026. The programme support
 s projects exploring the crossovers of art with science\, technology and e
 cology\, which makes it one of the stronger art-science fits in Europe. Re
 sidents receive a furnished live-work studio of around 50 m2 in Paris\, EU
 R 1\,000 per month living stipend\, up to EUR 3\,000 production budget\, r
 ound-trip travel and mentoring\, with residencies of 3 or 6 months for sol
 o artists and 3 months for duos of an artist with a researcher\, curator o
 r writer. Open to visual\, performing and digital artists of all nationali
 ties and ages with at least 5 years of professional experience and an inte
 rnational exhibition record. Programme details at artexplora.org. TO APPLY
 : submit via the Art Explora application platform. DEADLINE: 30 October 20
 26\, 11:59 PM Paris time.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation and Cit
 é internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France. Open worldwide to ar
 tists with at least 5 years of professional practice.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 p
 er month living stipend plus up to EUR 3\,000 production grant\, a furnish
 ed live-work studio of around 50 m2 at the Cité internationale des arts\,
  round-trip travel to Paris and curatorial mentoring. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 3- or 6-month residencies during 2027\; 3 months for duos (arti
 st plus researcher\, curator or writer).\n\nMore: https://artexplora.plate
 formecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years of
  professional practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:after-the-palace-resonance-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 Video Mapping Contest (K
 rakow)
DESCRIPTION:AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 is an international video mapp
 ing competition and outdoor showcase that asks digital media artists to cr
 eatively reinterpret the dissonant heritage of socialist-era architecture 
 in the context of the history\, cultural identity and memory of Krakow's N
 owa Huta. Artists\, animators\, motion designers\, creative teams and stud
 ios worldwide are invited to create original site-specific projections for
  the courtyard facade of Building Z of the New Administrative Centre\, for
 merly part of the Lenin Steelworks. Organised by the University of the Nat
 ional Education Commission in Krakow as part of the international artistic
  and research project unLoc. TECHNICAL: 2D/3D video mapping with sound\, 1
  to 8 minutes\, MP4 (H.264/AAC) in 4K at 25 fps\, minimum 40 Mbps\, audio 
 48 kHz/16-bit\, built on the dedicated building mapping matrix from the do
 cument package. Generative AI tools are permitted provided their use is fu
 lly disclosed in the application form and the applicant holds rights to th
 e source materials. TIMELINE: submission deadline 30 October 2026\, 23:59 
 CET\; results by 10 November\; outdoor showcase and award ceremony 23 Nove
 mber 2026 in the courtyard at 1 Ujastek St\, Krakow. TO APPLY: submit the 
 online application form with a download link to the work\; the full regula
 tions and mapping matrix are at unloc.art. Contact unloc@uken.krakow.pl.\n
 \nOrganisation: University of the National Education Commission in Krakow 
 (unLoc project)\nLocation: Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submis
 sion from anywhere\; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z
 \, New Administrative Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).\nAward: Cash prize
 s: PLN 10\,000 (~EUR 2\,340) first place\, PLN 6\,000 second\, PLN 3\,000 
 third\; the jury may award additional honorary distinctions or redistribut
 e the pool. Free to enter\, submission is exclusively digital.\n\nMore: ht
 tp://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submission from anywhere\
 ; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z\, New Administrati
 ve Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cnc-creation-immersive-2026-oct@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:Deadline: CNC: Fonds d'aide a la creation immersive (October 2026 s
 ession)
DESCRIPTION:The CNC's flagship fund for immersive creation (successor to DI
 CReAM since 2022): VR\, mixed reality and interactive narrative works\, as
 sessed by a commission chaired by Jean-Michel Jarre. Four strands cover th
 e whole chain: writing (ecriture)\, preproduction\, production and portage
  (bringing a finished work to audiences). AMOUNTS: the aid page states per
 centage caps rather than fixed sums\; CNC's published results pages for 20
 25 show writing grants of EUR 10\,000 to 12\,000\, preproduction up to EUR
  60\,000 and production up to EUR 80\,000. ELIGIBILITY: individual authors
  who are French nationals or legal residents of an EU/EEA state\, so Nethe
 rlands-based authors qualify\; companies and associations must be establis
 hed in France\; the project must be conceived/written in French and at lea
 st 50% of expenses must be in France. The fund runs four sessions per year
 \; this session closes 12 October 2026 (commission December 2026).\n\nOrga
 nisation: CNC (Centre national du cinema et de l'image animee)\nLocation: 
 France. Individual authors may be French nationals or residents of EU/EEA 
 states (Netherlands-based eligible)\; companies must be established in Fra
 nce\; writing must be in French and at least 50% of expenses spent in Fran
 ce.\nAward: Selective aid in four strands: ecriture\, preproduction\, prod
 uction and portage. The call page publishes percentage caps (up to 50% of 
 French financing\, 80% by derogation)\; CNC's own published commission res
 ults show ecriture grants of EUR 10\,000 to 12\,000\, preproduction up to 
 EUR 60\,000 and production up to EUR 80\,000. No application fee.\nDuratio
 n: Per project\n\nMore: https://www.cnc.fr/professionnels/aides-et-finance
 ments/creation-numerique/fonds-daide-a-la-creation-immersive_1725797?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.cnc.fr/professionnels/aides-et-financements/creation-numeri
 que/fonds-daide-a-la-creation-immersive_1725797?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:France. Individual authors may be French nationals or residents of
