UID:schaufler-residency-tu-dresden-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
SUMMARY:Deadline: Schaufler Residency@TU Dresden 2027 (six-month art and sc
 ience residency\, Energy Cultures in Transition)
DESCRIPTION:The Schaufler Lab at TUD Dresden University of Technology\, a j
 oint project with The Schaufler Foundation\, invites applications for its 
 six-month artist-in-residence at the interface of art and science for 2027
 . The theme of the Lab's third funding phase (2027 to 2030) is Energy Cult
 ures in Transition: how forms of energy and energy transitions shape and a
 re shaped by cultural practices\, value systems\, power relations\, enviro
 nmental relationships and imaginaries of the future. Residents work with t
 he researchers of the Schaufler Kolleg graduate college and the wider univ
 ersity\, with access to humanities\, natural-science and engineering labs\
 , and give lectures\, talks and workshops\, including a collaboration with
  the Dresden University of Fine Arts. Past residents include Quadrature\, 
 Mario Pfeifer\, Rosa Barba and Esmeralda Conde Ruiz. ELIGIBILITY: internat
 ionally active artists or artist groups in media art\, conceptual art\, pe
 rformance and related fields with completed international projects and exh
 ibitions\, an interest in exchange between artistic and scientific researc
 h\, and proficient German or English\; presence on site in Dresden is requ
 ired by arrangement. Apply with a form\, CV\, portfolio\, project proposal
  (up to 10\,000 characters)\, project plan with potential TUD collaborator
 s\, a three-minute video and a recent letter of recommendation\, as one PD
 F by email. The call is subject to final funding approval. Residency start
 s April 2027. DEADLINE: 9 November 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Schaufler Lab@TU
  Dresden (TUD Dresden University of Technology and The Schaufler Foundatio
 n)\nLocation: Dresden\, Germany. Studio on the TU Dresden campus\; on-site
  presence by arrangement.\nAward: Fellowship of EUR 3\,000 net per month f
 or six months (EUR 18\,000)\, plus a production grant of up to EUR 10\,000
  for a solo exhibition at the TUD University Gallery in autumn 2027\, a st
 udio on campus and help finding accommodation. No application fee.\nDurati
 on: Six months from April 2027.\n\nMore: https://tu-dresden.de/gsw/schaufl
 erlab/schaufler-residency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://tu-dresden.de/gsw/schauflerlab/schaufler-residency?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Dresden\, Germany. Studio on the TU Dresden campus\; on-site prese
 nce by arrangement.
END:VEVENT
