UID:traces-art-science-energypolis-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261025T090441Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: TRACES Art & Science @ Energypolis 2027: residency at the
  EPFL Laboratory for Energy Materials (Sion)
DESCRIPTION:TRACES is a new art and science residency run by the Foundation
  for the Sustainable Development of Mountain Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Vala
 is-Wallis\, Energypolis\, the City of Sion and the Canton of Valais. The 2
 027 pilot embeds one visual artist for three months in Prof. Sascha Feldma
 nn's Laboratory for Energy Materials at EPFL\, which works on light-matter
  interactions and soft semiconductors for flexible solar cells\, energy-ef
 ficient screens and emerging quantum technologies. The artist develops ori
 ginal work in dialogue with the lab around the energy transition and the m
 aterials of the future\, with studio and production space\, scientific men
 toring and a public final presentation on 15 April 2027. ELIGIBILITY: conf
 irmed\, professional international visual artists aged 25 or over who fini
 shed their studies at least two years ago and have at least two years of p
 rofessional practice\; applications in English or French with a letter of 
 intent (two A4 pages)\, portfolio and CV via the online form. Laureate sel
 ected 7 December 2026. DEADLINE: 22 November 2026\, 23:59 Swiss time (CET)
 .\n\nOrganisation: Foundation for the Sustainable Development of Mountain 
 Regions (FDDM) with EPFL Valais-Wallis\nLocation: Energypolis campus\, Sio
 n\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.\nAward: Artist stipend of CHF 2\,000 
 per month (CHF 6\,000 total) covering living and research costs\, housing 
 in Sion\, travel from home and back up to CHF 1\,500\, and a separate prod
 uction budget set by the curator. No application fee.\nDuration: Three mon
 ths\, 11 January to 18 April 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.traces-opencall.ch
 /en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.traces-opencall.ch/en?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Energypolis campus\, Sion\, Valais\, Switzerland. In person.
END:VEVENT
