 opment experience to co-create a walkable VRChat world conceived as a voya
 ge\, with 5 to 7 environments\, 3 to 5 avatars and optional NPC players\; 
 events\, social worlds and theatre pieces are not wanted. Three individual
  artists are selected and work together with a creative technologist\, eac
 h indicating the skills they bring (for example Unity development\, 3D art
 \, animation\, sound art or narrative writing) with portfolio examples. WH
 AT YOU GET: an artist fee of EUR 10\,000 gross per artist (EUR 6\,000 on s
 igning\, EUR 2\,000 after the Test Lab\, EUR 2\,000 at the end) and a prod
 uction budget of up to EUR 15\,000 gross for working hours or external ass
 istance. The residency is fully online from January to June 2027\, with a 
 Test Lab at L.E.V. Gijon in May 2027 and a premiere at L.E.V. Matadero in 
 September 2027\; no travel or accommodation is included. APPLICATION: onli
 ne form linked from the call page. DEADLINE (extended): 6 November 2026\, 
 23:59 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Realities in Transition (RiT2\, Creative Euro
 pe)\, with L.E.V. Festival\nLocation: Online residency\, with a Test Lab a
 t L.E.V. Gijon and a premiere at L.E.V. Matadero (Madrid)\, Spain. Check t
 he RiT residencies page for country eligibility.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 gross
  artist fee per selected artist (paid in three instalments) plus up to EUR
  15\,000 gross production budget shared among the team. No travel or accom
 modation included. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 6 months onlin
 e\, January to June 2027\; Test Lab in May 2027\, final presentation in Se
 ptember 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.realities-in-transition.eu/rit-2-open-c
 all-3/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
