DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Deadline: HIIG Impact AI Fellowship 2027 (EUR 5\,000\, 10 weeks\, B
 erlin and remote)
DESCRIPTION:HIIG's Impact AI Fellowship invites people interested in measur
 ing the effects of AI on society and the environment to assess an existing
 \, operational AI application and take lead authorship of a published case
  report. Applicants do not need their own case\; HIIG helps match fellows 
 with cases\, and proposed cases must be deployed applications rather than 
 prototypes or research ideas. WHO: holders of a master's degree\; field ex
 perience is an advantage but an academic track record is not required. FOR
 MAT: ten weeks from 16 August to 22 October 2027\, with mandatory in-perso
 n weeks in Berlin (16-20 August and 4-8 October 2027)\, an independent res
 earch phase that can be done remotely\, regular online check-ins\, and a m
 andatory online preparatory session on 11 May 2027. WHAT YOU GET: a fixed 
 EUR 5\,000 stipend and case-by-case partial support for in-person costs\; 
 health insurance\, visa and meals are the fellow's responsibility. APPLICA
 TION: online form with one combined file (CV up to 4 pages\, motivation le
 tter up to 2 pages\, optional project description up to 2 pages). Info ses
 sions on 10 November 2026 (10:00) and 17 November 2026 (15:00). DEADLINE: 
 15 January 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Alexander von Humboldt Institute for Int
 ernet and Society (HIIG)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany (two mandatory in-per
 son weeks\; other weeks can be remote). No nationality restriction stated.
 \nAward: EUR 5\,000 fixed stipend per fellow for the ten weeks (inclusive 
 of any tax or social security in the fellow's home country)\, with case-by
 -case partial support for in-person costs. No application fee mentioned.\n
 Duration: 10 weeks\, 16 August to 22 October 2027\, with in-person weeks i
 n Berlin on 16-20 August and 4-8 October 2027 and a mandatory online prepa
 ratory session on 11 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiig.de/en/impact-ai-c
 all-for-fellows/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hiig.de/en/impact-ai-call-for-fellows/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany (two mandatory in-person weeks\; other weeks can 
 be remote). No nationality restriction stated.
END:VEVENT
